ecture: sound as an emergency stop. Landing the deployed bytes unchanged means that main equals what runs, so a deployment from main cannot turn the archive back on.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Turning the archive off removes a provider path and adds none. No archive receipt is published while the archive is off.\n\nSimplification: the condition is indirect. It works because `null` is never `undefined`, so a reader can easily take it for a real check. Keep it only until AR-1 restores the original line, as the request says. Do not copy the pattern elsewhere.\n\nFor AR-1, on my own account: I approved AE-1 in a163da26 without checking how often the driver wakes. For the AR-1 head I will read the code that writes each wake. I will check the 60 s floor, the 3600 s cap, the count limit of 32 and the reset on progress from ruling dbbdea21. I will also check that a stored past wake from the old code slows down on its first pass, and compare the note's expected requests per hour for each Worker with the deployed level.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:045d2a5ea31d5a5bda35753b69691f1d4d990c9b","binding":"assigned","head":"16063746d4ec3a91e077a8f68900fa12b1401eed","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c16906409f7e67b3c832df95b63bb966f70e7d8d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:339c826716cb5e6246972f624e362f7c42728e3e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c16906409f7e67b3c832df95b63bb966f70e7d8d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}